        "chapter": "Cash Flow Statement",
        "concept_id": "accountancy:financing-disclosure-purpose",
        "body": "Why does the chapter say separate disclosure of cash flows from financing activities is useful?",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "It helps users predict claims on future cash flows by providers of funds."
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "It lets users determine the amount of cash generated by sales of goods."
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "It identifies whether the enterprise acquired long-term assets."
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "It measures the timing and certainty of all operating receipts."
          }
        ],
        "correct_answer": "C",
        "explanation": "The excerpt says separate financing disclosure is useful for predicting claims on future cash flows by providers of capital and borrowings. The keyed option instead describes a different activity and is not the stated reason.",
